import mundane theorem    stdlib/sums/sum-extended
import mundane theorem    stdlib/sums/sum-single

theorem sum-of-cubes
  note        By induction on n: adding (k + 1)³ to k²(k + 1)²/4 gives
              (k + 1)²(k + 2)²/4.
  let n ∈ ℕ                                                           (H1)
  then Σ(k = 1 to n) k³ = n²·(n + 1)²/4

let S(m) = Σ(j = 1 to m) j³, for m ∈ ℕ                                (D1)
       reads the sum of the first m cubes

1.  For all k ∈ ℕ, S(k) = k²·(k + 1)²/4.
    induction on k starting at 1

    base
    1.1.  Σ(j = 1 to 1) j³ = 1³
          mun:sum-single a := 1

    1.2.  S(1) = 1²·(1 + 1)²/4
          calculation
            S(1) = Σ(j = 1 to 1) j³     D1
                 = 1³                   1.1
                 = 1²·(1 + 1)²/4        arithmetic

    step
    let k ∈ ℕ                                                         (K)
    assume step 1 is true for k, the induction hypothesis             (IH)

    1.3.  Σ(j = 1 to k + 1) j³ = Σ(j = 1 to k) j³ + (k + 1)³
          mun:sum-extended a := 1, n := k
          requires k ≥ 1: from K

    1.4.  S(k + 1) = S(k) + (k + 1)³
          calculation
            S(k + 1) = Σ(j = 1 to k + 1) j³          D1
                     = Σ(j = 1 to k) j³ + (k + 1)³   1.3
                     = S(k) + (k + 1)³               D1

    1.5.  S(k) + (k + 1)³ = k²·(k + 1)²/4 + (k + 1)³
          substitute S(k) = k²·(k + 1)²/4 (IH)

    1.6.  k²·(k + 1)²/4 + (k + 1)³ = (k + 1)²·((k + 1) + 1)²/4
          algebra

    1.7.  S(k + 1) = (k + 1)²·((k + 1) + 1)²/4
          calculation
            S(k + 1) = S(k) + (k + 1)³                  1.4
                     = k²·(k + 1)²/4 + (k + 1)³         1.5
                     = (k + 1)²·((k + 1) + 1)²/4        1.6

2.  S(n) = n²·(n + 1)²/4
    instantiate k := n in line 1

3.  Σ(k = 1 to n) k³ = n²·(n + 1)²/4
    calculation
      Σ(k = 1 to n) k³ = S(n)             D1
                       = n²·(n + 1)²/4    2
